            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your patient, a 57-year-old male, admitted on 06/07/2023 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Spirometry supported the known obstructive ventilatory pattern. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. The patient was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebulizer, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in significant clinical improvement. Vital signs were monitored continuously throughout the stay. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. We recommend close follow-up and optimization of maintenance therapy.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
